# Gale-Stewart Infinite Game Theory: Core Foundations

Rigorous foundations for Gale-Stewart infinite games: strategies, plays,
winning conditions, determinacy, Wadge reducibility, game rank, quasi-strategies,
and game morphisms.

## References
* D. Gale, F.M. Stewart, "Infinite games with perfect information" (1953)
* D.A. Martin, "Borel Determinacy" (1975)
* A. Kechris, "Classical Descriptive Set Theory" (1995)
-/

namespace GS

open Classical

/-! ## Core Definitions -/

/-- A strategy in a Gale-Stewart game: maps finite play histories to moves. -/
def Strategy (α : Type*) := List α → α

/-- Build the finite prefix of a play from two strategies. -/
def playPrefix {α : Type*} (σ τ : Strategy α) : ℕ → List α
  | 0 => []
  | n + 1 =>
    let h := playPrefix σ τ n
    h ++ [if n % 2 = 0 then σ h else τ h]


/-- The infinite play generated by two strategies. -/
noncomputable def playOf {α : Type*} (σ τ : Strategy α) (n : ℕ) : α :=
  if n % 2 = 0 then σ (playPrefix σ τ n) else τ (playPrefix σ τ n)

/-! ## Winning Conditions and Determinacy -/

/-- Player I has a winning strategy for payoff set A. -/
def WinningI {α : Type*} (A : Set (ℕ → α)) : Prop :=
  ∃ σ : Strategy α, ∀ τ : Strategy α, playOf σ τ ∈ A

/-- Player II has a winning strategy for payoff set A. -/
def WinningII {α : Type*} (A : Set (ℕ → α)) : Prop :=
  ∃ τ : Strategy α, ∀ σ : Strategy α, playOf σ τ ∉ A

/-- A game G(A) is determined if one player has a winning strategy. -/
def Determined {α : Type*} (A : Set (ℕ → α)) : Prop :=
  WinningI A ∨ WinningII A

